think Read the compass first: KYRI.md and RADIANT_STYLE.md to be Kyri, then crux/REMEMBER.md, the top session-log recommends, REDS, and the Season G / Microkernel framing in the eight-season double-seat itinerary.
think Standfast check: walked crux/REDS.md living rows. 80, 83, 84, 85 closed; 86, 78, 81, 82, 87 released; only 75 rests as custody-gated errata (a deep debride, custody gate 1, Keaton's hand). No agent-closable red open -- Standfast clear, new work allowed.
think Lindy-first crux-first on the live green edge: the Microkernel double-seat leads yet its only ungated moves are research rounds behind a web-fetch/license gate (itinerary line 157 names them as un-searched, so no fact fabricated), surfaced not crossed. So the loop grows Season G open-media as it has.
think The hit-or-miss log named three siblings -- a corner/endpoint template pack, a disk-element builder, a thinning pass composed from hit-or-miss. Crux-first takes the thinning pass: the hardest-solvable and most Lindy (the floor skeletonization, pruning, and endpoint detection all descend from), a genuine iterate-to-fixed-point algorithm the other two ride on.
think Read the compose surface: image/hitmiss.rye (hit_or_miss returns a clean white-on-black match plane), image/structure.rye (StructuringElement, Offset, erode_se, structure_max_offsets), morphology_tophat.rye (the subtract_bytes idiom), qoi.rye (Pixmap, same_bytes, qoi_max_pixels = 1<<20 so the dynamic ceiling fits u32).
think Designed the crux before coding: thin_once(A, fg, bg) = A AND NOT hit_or_miss(A, fg, bg), a set difference. Because out_lit = on AND NOT matched <= on, a step can NEVER add a pixel (anti-extensive) for ANY template pair, so the on-set is a strictly decreasing bounded sequence and the fixed-point loop always terminates -- the productive-pass count is at most the initial foreground count, the ceiling the driver asserts.
think Chose a hand-verifiable convergence proof: the right-edge peel template (fg={center,left}, bg={right}) strips the rightmost column of every horizontal run one pass at a time. A 4-wide 3-tall solid block held clear of every border (so no clamp fakes a left neighbor) thins to its single leftmost column over EXACTLY three productive passes then converges -- computed by hand, asserted byte-for-byte.
obs Built image/thin.rye (thin_once the step, thin the fixed-point driver taking a passes-out counter) + tools/thin_witness.rish. GREEN on the first full metal run, no reds: definition crux (thin_once == binarized-source AND-NOT the match byte-for-byte against a hand-composed difference); anti-extensive (every lit output pixel was lit in the source); the fixed-point peel crux (block to one-pixel column, exactly three passes, converges); idempotence (already-thin skeleton, zero passes, same image); QOI round-trip; four refusals by name (empty foreground/background/source, over-max template) having allocated nothing; determinism in both pass count and pixels.
obs Compose not braid: this rung OWNS only the set difference (alpha pinned opaque so a thinned mask stays a clean plane) and the loop; hitmiss.hit_or_miss OWNS the match, structure the fit gather, qoi the buffers. The binary meaning of a pixel (red >= 128) is read from hitmiss.hitmiss_on_threshold, one source of truth. The guard mirrors hit_or_miss's refusals so the driver is all-or-nothing (no seed allocation on a refusal).
obs tame_style_check GREEN (bans clean), width-check exit 0, plain 7-bit ASCII in both new files, living_docs_lint advisory-GREEN, living_card_ascii_witness GREEN (operator card + REDS pure ASCII). image/README.md seats a Thin (to a skeleton) bullet after the hit-or-miss Detect entry (docs-sync). REMEMBER repointed single-stranded: the thin live-edge and git-nib written thin-first, hitmiss folded to the prior trail (no cairn -- a one-line repoint).
obs The `thin` name is a plain warm word (comlink tendency), colliding with nothing seated -- the LEXICON thin-edge / thin-implement senses are a different domain (the testing edge), and no module named thin existed.
